This section describes the course-authoring features used in CAT-SOOP page
source files.

<tableofcontents/>

<catsoop-section>Course Structure</catsoop-section>

* [Creating New Pages](CURRENT/pages) explains the course directory tree,
  `content.catsoop`, inherited `preload.py` settings, roles, and page dates.
* [Structure of a Course Page](CURRENT/page_structure) describes sections,
  subsections, includes, page Python, and questions.
* [Page Rendering and Request Data](CURRENT/rendering) explains mixed Markdown
  and HTML, the rendering pipeline, and request values in `cs_form`.
* [Images and Other Static Content](CURRENT/static_content) explains
  `__STATIC__`, images and downloads, and the `CURRENT`, `COURSE`, and `BASE`
  URL prefixes.
* [Dynamic Python-Generated Pages](CURRENT/dynamic_pages) explains
  `content.py`, request-driven output, `cs_handler`, raw responses, redirects,
  JSON and CSV endpoints, and staff-only page controls.
* [Defining Course Users](CURRENT/users) explains `__USERS__`, per-user Python
  files, roles, sections, identity fields, and other user metadata.

<catsoop-section>Question Types</catsoop-section>

Question types are embedded in a page with a
<code>&lt;question TYPE&gt;</code> block.
The following authoring references describe several commonly used question
types:

* [The `pythonic` question type](CURRENT/pythonic), for grading Python
  expressions, including multi-line expressions and several related input
  fields.
* [The `pythoncode` question type](CURRENT/pythoncode), for grading functions
  and programs with one or more sandboxed test cases.
* [The `checkoff` question type](CURRENT/checkoff), for staff-approved
  conversations, demonstrations, and lab milestones.

<catsoop-section>Extracting Information From CAT-SOOP's Logs</catsoop-section>

* [Reading CAT-SOOP Logs](CURRENT/logs) describes the on-disk layout, binary
  representation, command-line tools, and the `csm_cslog` Python API.
* [Problem Logs and Question Metadata](CURRENT/problem_logs) explains
  `problemactions`, `problemstate`, `_question_info`, asynchronous checker
  data, and how these records are used by course progress pages.
